          <declname>MI</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Return true if this is a floating-point store smaller than the V reg. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>On cyclone, these require a vector shuffle before storing a pair. Ideally we would call <ref refid="_a_arch64_load_store_optimizer_8cpp_1a2891bebbb2a99d3d169b71fd68a0cd87" kindref="member">getMatchingPairOpcode()</ref> and have the machine model tell us if it&apos;s profitable with no cpu knowledge here.</para>
<para>FIXME: We plan to develop a decent <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_target" kindref="compound">Target</ref> abstraction for simple loads and stores. Until then use a nasty switch similar to AArch64LoadStoreOptimizer. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
